This assert statement is checking if the amount being transferred (amnt) is greater than 0 and less or equal to 100. If the condition is not met, an AssertionError with the message "transfer amount should be not greater than 100 and is positive" will be raised.
--------------------```python
def outputs():
    p1 = Person("John")
    p2 = Person("Alice")
    assert(transfer(p1, p2, 50)) # Checks if 50 transfer is possible from John to Alice
    
    assert(not transfer(p2, p1, 150)) # Checks if 150 transfer is not possible from Alice to John as she doesn't have 150 in her accounts

    assert(not transfer(p1, p2, 120)) # Checks if 120 transfer is not possible from John to Alice as he doesn't have 120 in his accounts

    assert(transfer(p1, p2, 50)) # Checks if 50 transfer is possible from John to Alice as after 50 transfer from the previous test, his account had 50 money

outputs()
